    "created_at": "2026-11-16T19:24:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:24:02Z",
    "body": "<details><summary>Issue found by AI</summary>\r\nShould these controls follow the used or the computed value of 'direction'? \"Inline-start\" is defined by the used value, and `text-orientation: upright` makes the used value `ltr`. The old text used the computed value. So for `<input type=range style=\"writing-mode: vertical-lr; direction: rtl; text-orientation: upright\">` the lowest value moves from the bottom to the top, and likewise for `meter` and `progress`. That goes beyond the `sideways-lr` case this PR is about.\r\n\r\n- a: Keep as is, so the controls follow the text flow as CSS defines it. Firefox Nightly already does this for range; Chrome Canary would need to change for all three controls. This would need tests for the upright case.\r\n- b: Say that the sides are determined by the computed value of 'direction'. Chrome Canary already does this for all three controls; Firefox Nightly would need to change for range. It departs from how CSS defines inline-start.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Evidence</summary>\r\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes-4/#inline-start says:\r\n> For boxes with a used 'direction' value of ltr, this means the line-left side. For boxes with a used 'direction' value of rtl, this means the line-right side.\r\nand for `upright`, https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes-4/#valdef-text-orientation-upright says:\r\n> This value causes the used value of 'direction' to be ltr, and for the purposes of bidi reordering, causes all characters to be treated as strong LTR.\r\nWith `writing-mode: vertical-lr; direction: rtl; text-orientation: upright`:\r\n| | Chrome Canary 160 | Firefox Nightly 160 |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| range | starts at the bottom | starts at the top |\r\n| meter, progress | start at the bottom | render the same for `ltr` and `rtl` in vertical writing modes |\r\nI didn't test Safari.\r\n</details>\r\n<details><summary>Reviewed commits</summary>\r\nReviewed at 89b76b1 on 877d614, with web-platform-tests/wpt@7e4fe2d, using spec-pr-review.\r\n</details>",
