    "created_at": "2026-11-18T23:05:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T23:05:10Z",
    "body": "It seems likely to be an i18n improvement to use `inline-start` and `inline-end` instead of \"top\" and \"bottom\", but I don't know enough about the relevant cultures to know whether this will violate expectations in practice. Hopefully the requested i18n review will help answer that (and hopefully they give the answer that allows this simple solution). I'm less worried about the range, meter, and progress elements than I was about switches, because I haven't had the personal experience of struggling to figure out which direction is \"up\" for the more-continuous elements.",
